# Documents API walkthrough for the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the API (`pnpm dev:api`) and send the requests from top to bottom. No secret lives here:
# export these before starting the editor (the key is the browser-safe one from the root .env).
#   SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   KB_EMAIL   KB_PASSWORD

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@supabaseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:54321
@publishableKey = {{$processEnv SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
@email = {{$processEnv KB_EMAIL}}
@password = {{$processEnv KB_PASSWORD}}
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.access_token}}
@documentId = {{createDocument.response.body.$.id}}

### 0. Sign up once (the local stack signs the user in without an email confirmation)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 1. Sign in; later requests reuse the access token
# @name signIn
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Create a document → 201, embeddingStatus "pending"
# @name createDocument
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Release notes",
  "content": "# Release notes\n\n- Documents are searchable by title and tag.\n- Uploads accept .txt, .md and .pdf.",
  "tags": ["release", "q3"]
}

### 3. List: title search, tag and status filters, pagination with the total match count
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents?search=release&tag=q3&status=pending&limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Read one document, content included
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Change only the tags → the embedding status stays as it was
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tags": ["release", "q3", "shipped"] }

### 6. Change the content → embeddingStatus is "pending" again and updatedAt moves
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "# Release notes\n\n- Uploads now keep the original filename." }

### 7. Upload Markdown → 201 with sourceType "upload", titled after the file
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=KbBoundary

--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

walkthrough
--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="meeting-notes.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# Meeting notes

Decisions are recorded in DECISIONS.md.
--KbBoundary--

### 8. Upload a PDF with an explicit title (one line break between pages in the text)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=KbBoundary

--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Two-page sample
--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="two-pages.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../apps/api/__tests__/fixtures/two-pages.pdf
--KbBoundary--

### 9. A PDF without a text layer (a scan, say) → 422 invalid_payload
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=KbBoundary

--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="no-text.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../apps/api/__tests__/fixtures/no-text.pdf
--KbBoundary--

### 10. Any other file type → 415 unsupported_media_type (files over 10 MiB get 413)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=KbBoundary

--KbBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="setup.exe"
Content-Type: application/x-msdownload

MZ
--KbBoundary--

### 11. An invalid body → 422 with per-field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "tags": ["a tag that is far too long to be accepted by the API"] }

### 12. Re-index one document → { "queued": 1 }; 0 while it is being indexed (3 requests a minute)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}/reindex
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Re-index every document of the caller → { "queued": n }
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/reindex-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Delete → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. The deleted document (or another user's) → 404 not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{documentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
